{
  "id": 314035420,
  "iid": 16361,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Thrift: fix incorrect proto_depth calculation",
  "description": "In case a sub-dissector handles a command containing structures, the\ncurrent depth was not incremented for the content of the structure\nitself and, more importantly, was improperly decremented when exiting\nthe structure.\nIn most cases, the bug could be hidden by the parent element correctly\nresetting the value to its expected current state but when the structure\nis the element type of a container (list, set, map), the sequence of\nstructures would decrement the count below 0, resulting in an underflow\nthat triggers the ei_thrift_too_many_subtypes expert info.\n\nThis issue does not affect the standard Thrift dissector that follows a\ndifferent path.\n\nNote 1: It can be tested with [this capture](https://gitlab.com/-/project/7898047/uploads/99d63eaf8a2780a1da96cb111267deea/anony-tcp-std.pcap) and the sub-dissector from [the armeria branch on my fork](https://gitlab.com/EnigmaTriton/wireshark/-/tree/armeria), it happens from frame 46 and the `someone_tries_to_analyze` command.\n\nNote 2: The issue exists on 4.2.5 and the patch can be applied on the 4.2 branch (in fact, I developed it and tested it there first) so it would be good to apply it as well for current sub-dissectors using the stable version. Thanks.",
  "state": "merged",
